			"notes": "## 1.1.5 - MccInfo Chat Fix & Badges\n\n### New\n- **Mcc JEI**: new Utils option. Turn it off to hide the item list, its search bar, the Switch Items toggle and Recipe Mode in inventories.\n- **Show My Mod Badge**: new Utils option. Turn it off and other MccInfo players no longer see the mod icon next to your name in the Tab list; you no longer see theirs either.\n- **See Others' Mod Badges**: new Utils option. Turn it off to hide the mod icon of other players in your Tab list.\n- **Api Key page**: new page at the bottom of the menu, to save your own MCC Island API key for upcoming features (with a button to get one on the Noxcrew Gateway). It is kept only on your computer. (useless for the moment)\n\n### Changes\n- **MccInfo Chat names**: ranks, crowns, factions and MCC+ of the players now come from the MCC Island API instead of the Tab list, so nobody can fake them. No Api Key needed: everyone gets the styled names.\n- **Tab badges**: the mod icons next to the names in the Tab list have a new texture, and they are now sent by the MccInfo server, so they can be updated without a new version of the mod.\n- **Vendor NPCs in recipes**: the NPC next to a vendor now shows its name in gold in a box above it, and the area where to find it in a box below it (the < 1/x > arrows are under the area).\n\n### Fixes\n- **Compact Fishing Messages**: Triggered and You earned lines that arrived before their catch, or late because of lag, were sometimes left as separate lines; they are now added to the right catch line. (found by humiebees)\n- **Shared items in the MccInfo chat**: they are now easy to hover, the whole icon shows the tooltip instead of a few pixels on its left.\n- **Centered text**: text in the item list and recipe boxes (Previous, Next, < 1/x >...) and the unread count next to the MCCINFO and MOD chat buttons are now centered."
		},
