			"notes": "## 1.1.4 - Emotes Update\n\n### Changes\n- **Shared emote music**: when several players play the same emote next to each other, only the first one's music plays; the others fade back in, in time, once they move apart. If you arrive while an emote is playing, its music now starts at the right moment instead of from the beginning.\n- **Smoother emotes**: the body now moves smoothly into the emote pose (the animation starts a few tenths of a second later) and smoothly back to normal when it stops, instead of snapping.\n- **First person**: your own emote no longer shows its 3D models, mirage or air bands in front of your camera; particles and shockwaves are still shown.\n\n### Fixes\n- **Emote sound range**: stereo music could be heard at full volume from anywhere on the map; emote sounds are now only heard near the player playing them.\n- **Emote sound direction**: music and sounds now come from the direction of the player playing the emote, instead of always sounding centered. While you play an emote, its music stays centered for you and for everyone playing the same emote with you.\n- **Voice chat volumes**: changing the volume of a player, or of all other players, now actually changes what you hear."
		},
